nova: Precheck for a host virtlogd

nova_libvirt runs its own virtlogd and shares the host's /run, so a
virtlogd running or enabled on the host conflicts with it and, with
older images, makes instance creation fail as libvirt sends console
logs to a virtlogd that cannot see the instance directories.

Fail prechecks when the host's virtlogd units are active or enabled.
Unlike the host libvirt check, run this on existing deployments too,
since the conflict only matters once console logs go via virtlogd.

Prompt: interactive debugging of an upgrade error report from ``Vii``
on the #openstack-kolla IRC channel.

